  en: {
    series: `Avatar Tips #${article.no}`,
    title: "When a gimmick doesn't work",
    lead: "You press it in the menu and nothing happens. Only you can see it. It resets when you change worlds. When a gimmick doesn't work the way you expected, this page shows where to start, what order to check things in, and a list of common causes. When you're stuck, come here first.",
    meta: "This covers Unity's Built-in Render Pipeline and VRChat avatars (Avatars 3.0). Up to date as of November 2026.",
    publishedLabel: "Published",
    tocLabel: "Contents",
    whenTitle: "Read this when",
    when: [
      "A gimmick you built doesn't do anything when you press it in the menu.",
      "You can see it, but someone told you they can't.",
      "Your toggles reset when you change worlds or switch avatars.",
      "It worked in Unity, but it doesn't work in VRChat.",
      "You can't tell what's wrong, and you don't know where to start looking.",
    ],
    orderTitle: "The order to check things",
    orderLead: [
      "A gimmick works by passing a value along in this order: <strong>menu → parameter → state → clip → what you see</strong> (for details, see " + to("animator-basics", "picture") + "). If it stops being passed along somewhere, nothing after that point works.",
      "So <strong>start at the front and check, one step at a time, how far the value gets</strong>. The cause is just before the point where it stops. This finds the problem much faster than fixing whatever comes to mind.",
      "And <strong>check in Unity first</strong>. To test in VRChat, you have to upload and wait every time. In Unity, you just fix it and press Play, and you can check right away.",
    ],
    route: [
      { head: "1. Play in Unity", note: "Press the menu in Gesture Manager" },
      { head: "2. Parameter", note: "Does the value change?" },
      { head: "3. State", note: "Does it go into a different state?" },
      { head: "4. Clip", note: "Is it writing the right things?" },
      { head: "5. Yourself in VRChat", note: "Upload and try it" },
      { head: "6. With friends", note: "Can other people see it?" },
    ],
    orderStepsTitle: "What to look at in each step, and where to look when it stops",
    orderSteps: [
      { head: "1. Play in Unity with Gesture Manager",
        body: "Follow the steps in the next section: press Unity's Play button, then press the gimmick's item in the Gesture Manager menu. If it works in Unity, your Animator and clips are set up correctly. Go on to 5. If it doesn't work in Unity either, check from 2 in order." },
      { head: "2. Does the parameter's value change?",
        body: "When you press the menu, look at the Debug section of Gesture Manager and see whether that parameter's value changes. <strong>If it doesn't change, the cause is the menu or Expression Parameters</strong>. Check that the names match, and that the parameter is in Expression Parameters." },
      { head: "3. Does it go into a different state?",
        body: "If the parameter changes but the state doesn't, the cause is <strong>the parameter name in the Animator, or the transition conditions</strong>. In the Animator window, look at which state is running in that layer (how to look is in the next section)." },
      { head: "4. Is the clip writing the right things?",
        body: "If the state changes but what you see doesn't, the cause is <strong>what's in the clip, or the layer settings</strong>. Check that the clip's paths aren't broken (Missing), that the layer's Weight isn't 0, and that a lower layer isn't writing the same thing." },
      { head: "5. Check it yourself in VRChat",
        body: "Once it works in Unity, upload and try it in VRChat. If it works in Unity but not in VRChat, look at <strong>things that were removed during upload</strong> (such as EditorOnly objects), and at which avatar you uploaded to." },
      { head: "6. Ask a friend how it looks to other people",
        body: "Once it works for you, ask a friend to look. Gesture Manager and your own screen can only show you <strong>how you see yourself</strong>. If other people can't see it, check the parameter's Synced setting (sends it to other people) and the Quest version." },
    ],
    orderNote: "Once you know which step it stops at, pick that problem in the \"Common causes\" list below to narrow down where to look.",
    toolsTitle: "Tools for checking",
    toolsLead: "There are three main tools for checking: Gesture Manager in Unity, the Animator window in Unity, and the displays inside VRChat.",
    gmTitle: "Gesture Manager (run it like VRChat, in Unity)",
    gmLead: [
      `Gesture Manager is a tool that runs your avatar's Animator in Unity Play mode the same way VRChat does. You can try out your menu (Expressions Menu) and hand gestures inside Unity. It's made by BlackStartx (${ext(links.gestureManager, "Gesture Manager download page")}).`,
      `Add Gesture Manager to your project from the project list in VCC or ALCOM. For how to add it, see ${to("setup", "packages")}.`,
